      "writtenOn": "2024-08-22T20:54:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think KTX decoding is wired up at all: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/skia/src/codec/SkAndroidCodec.cpp;l\u003d242;drc\u003d9334913e878d64842aa752009f57fec5acf080dc\n\nCan you describe the use-case + need for supporting KTX bitmaps?",
      "revId": "1b522bde57384c09b6a0aecc28950b2d19a9437d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4b786df0_cd89c9fd",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3524514
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-29T09:35:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hey @alecmouri@google.com, regarding our use case \u0026 need for supporting KTX bitmaps see below:\n\nKTX bitmaps are needed for using ASTC-compressed resources. As of right now from our testing we found out AOSP is not the most efficient when it comes to memory usage on that front, and that it is massively wasteful of memory and performance to use anything other than compressed resources for rendering.",
      "parentUuid": "564845ed_87ec2d66",
      "revId": "1b522bde57384c09b6a0aecc28950b2d19a9437d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9902d1e3_0c77facd",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1470474
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-29T15:03:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What sort of applications are you imagining using ASTC resources?",
      "parentUuid": "4b786df0_cd89c9fd",
      "revId": "1b522bde57384c09b6a0aecc28950b2d19a9437d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e5bacef_5b2f8df6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3524514
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-29T17:06:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Pretty much all of them if not as many as we can. The reasoning for using KTX bitmaps and ASTC-compressed resources is that the memory usage by uncompressed resources is too high to justify. Even if a single PNG or JPG file may be relatively small, the resource used by composition is full size and 32 bpp, which can add up quickly. By using KTX resources you only keep one copy (the hardware one) and its compressed resource, resulting in smaller resident size in memory and higher performance when compositing. While this may increase the APK size, it is a trade-off worth making for the benefits in memory usage and performance.",
      "parentUuid": "9902d1e3_0c77facd",
      "revId": "1b522bde57384c09b6a0aecc28950b2d19a9437d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8c4505e9_f17ce55f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1470474
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T16:39:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So one immediate problem is that the non-HARDWARE bitmap configs are all uncompressed representations, and that will not be easy to change since the Bitmap api supports software rasterization + pixel retrieval.\n\nAnd, if you\u0027re decoding a bitmap with the HARDWARE config, then the uncompressed representation would only be used as intermediate memory during decoding. The final decoded result is transferred into a hardware resource which I would expect to be swizzled + compressed, and the uncompressed resource is thrown away.\n\nSo in practice, support through these apis won\u0027t buy you much. I\u0027m sympathetic to supporting decoding for interopability reasons (which would require Skia to agree to any changes), but the practical result of most apps using KTX resources would likely result in inflating their apk cost.",
      "parentUuid": "9e5bacef_5b2f8df6",
      "revId": "1b522bde57384c09b6a0aecc28950b2d19a9437d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
